  "summary": "Recent work applying federated or decentralised learning to churn prediction includes Brennan et al.'s federated learning deployment on the GEFCom dataset achieving an AUROC of 0.905 [D0023]. Iyer et al. report a decentralised update approach on SentinelYield-2 with a MAPE of 0.8 [D0022], while Okafor et al. use privacy-preserving cross‑institution training on MIMIC‑IV and obtain an F1 of 0.711 [D0021]. Lindqvist et al. evaluate a similar decentralised scheme on GEFCom, reporting 0.704 accuracy [D0024]. Although not federated, Lindqvist's graph‑neural‑network model for subscriber cancellations on SentinelYield-2 reaches an AUROC of 0.966, highlighting the strong baseline performance of non‑federated methods [D0025].",
